MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 3acd12a18dafdb74ab8b1dd16427d1e6, type: 3}
  m_Name: lines_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp-firstpass::NarrationScriptData
  lines:
  - Is anyone there? Hello?
  - Hey, are you okay?
  - You are now in dialogue mode. When you switch modes, the game will tell you which
    mode you're in. When the game is waiting for your input, you'll hear this sound.
    Press X, the bottom of the four buttons on the right side of your controller,
    to continue.
  - Press X, the lowest of the four buttons on the right side of your controller.
  - As long as there is text on the screen, you can navigate it using the up and
    down arrow keys on the left side of your controller and select it with X or the
    right arrow key. When you reach the top or bottom of the text, you'll hear this
    sound. Give it a try!
  - Press the up and down arrow buttons to navigate the text on the screen.
  - Great, one more thing. If you want to repeat the last sentence, press Square,
    the leftmost of the four buttons on the right side of the controller.
  - Press Square, the leftmost of the four buttons on the right side of the controller.
  - Dialog
  - Puzzle
  - Move
  - Menu
  - Wait for another person
  - Cutscene
  - Come on, get up.
  - Oh, I don't think your glasses survived the earthquake. Well, at least you seem
    to be unharmed.
  - There's no one else here but us. Let's go look for the others together.
  - Your friend is surely out there somewhere, just like the rest of my bandmates.
  - I'll follow you!
  - Use the left joystick to move. If you move the joystick to the left, your character
    moves to the left.
  - "Use the right joystick to change the direction you're facing. If you move it
    to the right once, you turn 90\xB0 to the right. Give it a try!"
  - Move with the left joystick and change your viewing direction with the right
    joystick.
  - Great. To help you know where you are even in enclosed spaces, there are three
    types of sounds.
  - When you run into a wall, you'll hear this sound.
  - When you walk along a wall, you'll hear this sound.
  - When there's a hallway to your left or right, you'll hear the sound of wind in
    your left or right ear.
  - One last thing.
  - When you're near an object you can interact with, this sound will play as long
    as you can interact with it.
  - Press the rear right button on the right side to interact with the object.
  - You are now in a room with an exit. Find the door you can interact with, then
    press the rear right button.
  - Great, you found the exit. Next time, the door won't open so easily. Good luck!
